format 1

# Seeded by `pklith seed --init` from the fragments this repository's
# files switch on (`pklith detect`). It is yours now: pklith never rewrites it.
#
# Edited by hand since (root T3): envrc gets shellcheck by type; gitignore is
# exempt; flake locks get the lock-graph guard (gate T1).
#
# Not laid, with its reason:
# - itok: `.context-limits` holds sherd's chain ceilings (`paradigm/V12`);
#   itok reads the same file as per-file ceilings and refuses root SPEC.md
#   above its 2,700 chain ceiling (paradigm T14). sherd-budget gates it.

## checks
id|category|nix|glob|check|fix|env|msg
# Root V1 on every tracked flake lock, root and dev (gate T1, gate V1).
lock-graph|supply|jq|**/flake.lock, gate/lock-graph.sh, gate/lock-graph.jq|git ls-files -z '*flake.lock' \| xargs -0 -n1 bash gate/lock-graph.sh|-|-|a flake lock holds more or fewer than one nixpkgs, or an input locks its own (root V1)
# The whole bats suite at push, so a RED commit can land (`docs/SHELL.md`).
# pklith v0.1.0 puts only the `coverage` category in hk.pklith.pkl's `push`
# mapping, hence the category; pklith main ships this row.
# Private names never reach a commit (gate T3, root V8, paradigm/V37).
name-guard|gate|gnugrep|**/*|bash gate/name-guard.sh {{files}}|-|-|a private name is staged (root V8); the hit names the denylist entry, never the name
bats-unit|coverage|bats|-|bats --recursive tests|-|-|a bats test under tests/ failed, or there is no tests/ directory
# Overrides the catalog row: bats files are bash too (`docs/SHELL.md`).
shellcheck|lint|shellcheck|**/*.sh, **/*.bash, **/*.bats, .envrc|shellcheck {{files}}|-|-|shell script finding
# Overrides the catalog row: shfmt reads bats from the extension.
shfmt|format|shfmt|**/*.sh, **/*.bash, **/*.bats|shfmt --diff {{files}}|shfmt --write {{files}}|-|shell script not formatted
# Every JSON file parses; pkgs/pnpm/sources.json is the first (pkgs T1).
json|lint|jq|**/*.json|jq -e . {{files}} >/dev/null|-|-|a JSON file does not parse

# The registry judges itself: generated steps match .pklith.
gen-check|gate|-|.pklith, hk.pklith.pkl, nix/pklith.nix|pklith gen --check|pklith gen|-|hk.pklith.pkl or nix/pklith.nix no longer matches .pklith; run `pklith gen`
# core.worktree in the shared .git/config would point every worktree at
# one checkout; `sherd wave` (root T5) runs parallel worktrees (paradigm/V15).
no-core-worktree|gate|git|-|test -z "$(git config --local --get core.worktree)"|-|-|core.worktree is set in the shared .git/config, so every worktree acts on one checkout (paradigm/V15)

# The gate is complete, fresh, runnable, and has steps (paradigm/V22).
confirm|gate|-|-|pklith confirm|-|-|the gate is incomplete, stale, unrunnable or evaluates to no steps (paradigm/V22)
# Every tracked file has a type, no row is stale, every claim reaches its
# files, and the mirror rules hold.
pklith-check|gate|-|-|pklith check|-|-|a tracked file type has no row in .pklith, a row matches nothing, a claimed check never reaches its files, or a mirror rule fails

## types
type|checks|min|exempt
*|name-guard, no-core-worktree, trailing-whitespace, final-newline, line-endings, no-bom, no-merge-conflict, no-case-conflict, no-broken-symlinks, no-private-key, ripsecrets, typos, editorconfig-checker, no-local-paths|-|-
bats|bats-parse, shellcheck, shfmt, bats-unit|-|-
editorconfig|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
gitattributes|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
md|markdownlint|-|-
nix|nixfmt, statix, deadnix|-|-
path:**/SPEC.md|markdownlint, mth-fmt, mth-check, sherd-check, sherd-nav, sherd-budget|-|-
path:.context-limits|sherd-budget|-|-
envrc|shellcheck|-|-
gitignore|-|-|ignore patterns, no linter reads them
markdownlintignore|-|-|ignore patterns, no linter reads them
toml|-|-|typos config; typos reads it on every run, a bad line fails the typos step
yaml|-|-|markdownlint config; yamllint lands with the workflows (root T4)
lock|lock-graph|-|-
pklith|gen-check, pklith-check, confirm|-|-
pkl|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
pre-commit|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
pre-push|-|-|written by pklith (seed or gen)
sh|shellcheck, shfmt|-|-
jq|-|-|jq program run by its shell script; that script's bats test runs it
json|json|-|-

## rules
id|kind|select|target|except
# Mirrored tests both ways (`docs/SHELL.md`): every script has its bats
# file, and no bats file outlives its script. Rows for scripts/ and
# checks/ land with their first script. TDD order waits for a pklith tag
# with the `tdd-order` kind (v0.1.0 has none).
dev-test|exists|dev/*.sh|tests/unit/dev/{stem}.bats|-
dev-orphan|orphan|tests/unit/dev/*.bats|dev/{stem}.sh|-
gate-test|exists|gate/*.sh|tests/unit/gate/{stem}.bats|-
gate-orphan|orphan|tests/unit/gate/*.bats|gate/{stem}.sh|-
scripts-test|exists|scripts/*.sh|tests/unit/scripts/{stem}.bats|-
scripts-orphan|orphan|tests/unit/scripts/*.bats|scripts/{stem}.sh|-
